  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 146 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nThrough Sunday: As the remnants of Isaias continues lifting away \nfrom the CWA, the drier air wrapping into the system will end the \nrainfall early this evening and the strong gusty winds will \ngradually subside. Thus, the Wind Advisory will be allowed to \nexpire. A surface high will become centered over the central Gulf \ncoast as a ridge aloft moves into our region from the west. This \nwill lead to warmer than normal temperatures with the warmest \ntemperatures in the west. Temperatures in the lower 90s will lead to \nlow relative humidity again but the wind will be much lighter and \nmitigate fire danger concerns. /22/\n\nSunday night-Friday:\n\nUpper-lvl high will build over the southeast CONUS and slowly move \neastward over the period. Dry conditions are expected throughout the \nweek as RH values fall to the upper 20s-30% near the MS Delta and \nwest of I-55 Sunday and Monday resulting in fire weather concerns to \nover those days. RH's are expected to increase above 30% over the \nweek but conditions will remain dry. Highs/lows temps will remain \nwell above-average through the end of the week. A cold front will \npush into the area into the weekend, dropping temps closer to \nseasonal averages. /SW/",
